From: =?UTF-8?q?Marko=20Banus=CC=8Cic=CC=81?= <mbanusic@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:55:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build_ipa_from_nsp.py: --icon picks the app's icon instead of
 the game's own

A built app's icon is always the game's icon.jpg from its control data. A player
who wants another picture (the game has none, as a dump folder does, or they
prefer a different one) has no way to set it for a Mac app: DM_ICON reaches only
build_ipa.sh, and pack_app.py takes --icon only from the NSP script.

--icon IMAGE names a PNG, JPEG or HEIC picture. app_icon() returns it instead of
the game's icon.jpg, and the NSP script hands it on as before: to pack_app.py's
--icon for --platform mac-app (sips and iconutil turn it into AppIcon.icns, and
the app's input key changes with it, so a reused app is packed again) and as
DM_ICON for the IPA. A path that is not a file stops the build with its name.
Without --icon nothing changes.

Checked: dm/tools/tests/test_nsp_mac_app.py and test_docs.py (76 tests) on
Python 3.15, two new tests for the option and the choice. lint_python.py has no
new finding in the changed files.

Front-ends: new: --icon IMAGE sets the built app's icon (IPA and Mac app)

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Th2dEas7VEirfhogR7VK5Y

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1380
Reason: the launcher's App icon tab (LNPANDY/NX2Apple#775) passes --icon for a Mac app or a one-game IPA before upstream merges it
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#775
